					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "CURVE\n\nThe Curve node takes a value between 0 and 1 and interpolate value between its min and max, calculated by the selected curve algorithm. What this means in practice is that the Curve node can be used for cool smoothing and animation.\n\nNote that some of the wilder algorithms like Bounce don't listen very strictly to your Min and Max values, they sort of do, but in their own rebellious way.\nAlso keep in mind that the Curve node wants a value from 0 to 1, giving values out of bounds will give weird results."
					}
				},
