			"40": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: THE CURVES\n\nIn this example we're simply demonstrating all the curves at once.\nThe Sequence node is used to select all the 22 different curves.\nWe added a bit of feedback by patching the video mixer back into itself, creating a trail effect."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 679.34552001953125,
					"width": 1604.806884765625,
					"x": 348.3675537109375,
					"y": 206.84405517578125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "fff26eb5",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"41": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 3: CUSTOM CURVES\n\nSo what if the curve you need is not in the curve node? You might need some kind of custom curve.\nThis example demonstrates how to create your own Curve node, without actually using the Curve node.\n\nWe start with a collection of floats, these are the points we're interpolating between.\nWe take the Size of the float collection and Map our slider from 0 to the size of the collection.\nNext, we read from the collection based on the position of our slider.\nNote that the Read node is set to Linear Interpolation.\nFinally we map the 0 to 1 range of the collection to whatever range we need with a second Map node."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 679.34552001953125,
					"width": 2030.31298828125,
					"x": 346.92041015625,
					"y": 940.7357177734375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffe53357",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"42": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 1: BASIC OPERATION\n\nIn this example we are moving a circle from left to right using a Float In node.\nThe float value from the Float In is 0 to 1. Next, the curve node turns this into -1 to 1 float with the given curve.\n\nTry changing the curve on the Curve node and play with the slider to see the different curve behaviors."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 367.203094482421875,
					"width": 984.2457275390625,
